The wording could probably be better and that sentence could be somewhere else, but I think we need to explicitly say somewhere that calling a function on Commands will only add a Command to the queue. It's implied by everything else, but anything that is implied is something that beginners might not understand.

```suggestion
///
/// In most cases a method is only going to add a Command to the queue, it won't be instantly applied.
///
```
